# send/send_all alias binding is case-sensitive while heartbeat/register compares are case-insensitive

## Steps to Reproduce

1. TODO: Add steps

## Expected Behavior

TODO: Describe expected behavior

## Actual Behavior

TODO: Describe actual behavior

## Symptom

Alias case handling is inconsistent across the B293 family: heartbeat/inbox_read owner compares and registers is_lease_refresh are case-insensitive, but /send and /send_all compare the signer against the body from_alias byte-exactly (relay.ml:5577-5579, 5637-5639). A client whose Authorization-header alias casing differs from its body from_alias gets 403 signature_invalid on send while heartbeat succeeds. Note the outer verifier (identity_pk_of, relay.ml:6897) still keys by exact case, so case-insensitivity only helps when the header matches the stored case.

## Fix direction

Use the lowercase compare in the send-family binding too, and normalize the binding lookup.

## Evidence

Server-core review 2026-09-17.